---
export const prerender = true;

import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="What data PapaBlog collects — currently, none."
  lastUpdated={new Date('2026-09-27')}
>
  <p>
    <strong>Short version:</strong> this site currently collects no personal data about visitors. There are no cookies,
    no analytics, no tracking scripts, and no forms to submit.
  </p>

  <h2>What this site does today</h2>
  <p>
    PapaBlog is a static blog. Pages are served directly with no visitor tracking, no advertising, and no third-party
    embeds that set cookies. Your hosting provider (Cloudflare) processes standard connection-level data (like IP
    address) to serve the page, as any web host does — this isn't something the site itself collects or has access to.
  </p>

  <h2>This will change as the site grows</h2>
  <p>
    Planned features — like a newsletter signup or privacy-respecting analytics — will collect some data (for example,
    an email address for double opt-in newsletter subscription). Before any such feature ships, this policy will be
    updated first to explain exactly what's collected, why, how long it's kept, and how to request it be deleted, in
    line with GDPR. The "Last updated" date above will change whenever that happens — check back if you want the current
    state.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about privacy on this site: <a href="mailto:dursky.k@gmail.com">dursky.k@gmail.com</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
